<div class="question" id="q1">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">1</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">Which of the following is the correct definition of <em>nutrition</em> in living organisms?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q1','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> The process of releasing energy from glucose in cells</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q1','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> The means of obtaining food that provides energy and molecules for living material</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q1','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> The elimination of waste products from the body</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q1','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> The process of breathing air into the lungs</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q1"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q2">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">2</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">Green plants are described as <em>autotrophic</em>. Which statement best explains this term?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q2','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> They obtain food from a range of different sources</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q2','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> They feed on decaying organic matter</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q2','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> They build up their own food using energy from the Sun</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q2','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> They absorb digested nutrients from other organisms</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q2"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q3">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">3</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">Respiration must not be confused with breathing. Which of the following correctly describes respiration?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q3','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> The physical process of moving air into and out of the lungs</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q3','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> The exchange of oxygen and carbon dioxide at the lung surface</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q3','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> A series of chemical reactions in cells that release energy stored in glucose</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q3','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> The transport of oxygen in red blood cells around the body</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q3"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q4">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">4</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">A student confuses egestion with excretion. Which of the following correctly distinguishes them?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q4','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> Excretion removes undigested food; egestion removes metabolic waste</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q4','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> Egestion removes faeces; excretion removes metabolic waste products such as urea</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q4','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> Both egestion and excretion describe the removal of urea from the kidney</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q4','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> Egestion and excretion are the same process in animals</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q4"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q5">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">5</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">The term <em>homeostasis</em> refers to which of the following?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q5','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> The process by which organisms reproduce sexually</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q5','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> The maintenance of a constant internal environment within required limits</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q5','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> The growth and development from a zygote to an adult</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q5','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> The movement of organisms from one habitat to another</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q5"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q6">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">6</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">Which of the following is an example of <em>asexual</em> reproduction?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q6','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> A flower producing seeds after pollination</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q6','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> A microscopic organism dividing into two</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q6','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> A male and female sex cell joining together</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q6','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> The transfer of pollen between two plants</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q6"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q7">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">7</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">State <strong>two</strong> differences in the way that plants and animals respond to stimuli in their environment. <span class="marks-guide">(Write your answer below)</span></div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Short answer</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[2]</div>
  </div>
  <textarea placeholder="Write your answer here..."></textarea>
  <button class="submit-btn" onclick="showModelAnswer(this, 'Plants respond slowly by growing towards/away from stimuli (e.g. light/gravity). Animals respond quickly using a nervous system and muscles/receptors. Plants do not have a nervous system or receptors. Animals can move their whole body (locomotion); plants usually only move parts of themselves.')">Show model answer</button>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q8">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">8</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">The table below refers to processes carried out by living organisms. Complete the table by ticking the correct boxes.</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Table completion</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[4]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="table-q">
    <table>
      <tr><th>Process / Statement</th><th style="text-align:center">Plants only</th><th style="text-align:center">Animals only</th><th style="text-align:center">Both</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Release energy from glucose using oxygen</td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Synthesise sugars using energy from sunlight</td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Use muscles to move from place to place</td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Excrete nitrogenous waste from protein breakdown</td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td><td class="tick-cell"><input type="checkbox"></td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>
  <button class="submit-btn" onclick="showModelAnswer(this, 'Row 1: Both ✓ | Row 2: Plants only ✓ | Row 3: Animals only ✓ | Row 4: Animals only ✓')">Show answers</button>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q9">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">9</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">Explain why the stomata of a plant leaf may close on a very hot, dry day and describe the effect this has on the leaf temperature.</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Extended writing</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[3]</div>
  </div>
  <textarea placeholder="Write your answer here..."></textarea>
  <button class="submit-btn" onclick="showModelAnswer(this, '• Stomata close to prevent further water loss / to conserve water [1]\n• This is because the plant is losing a lot of water by evaporation from leaves (transpiration) and may wilt if more is lost [1]\n• When stomata are open, evaporation of water cools the leaf (similar to sweating); closing the stomata means the leaf cannot cool itself as effectively, so leaf temperature rises [1]')">Show model answer</button>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q10">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">10</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">Which row of the table correctly matches the characteristic to its description?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q10','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> Excretion — the removal of undigested food from the gut as faeces</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q10','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> Respiration — the physical movement of air into and out of the lungs</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q10','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> Reproduction — the production of offspring to continue the species</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q10','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> Nutrition — the elimination of toxic metabolic waste products</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q10"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q11">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">11</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">In sexual reproduction, a new individual begins as a single fertilised egg cell called a <em>zygote</em>. State the name of the molecule that controls the characteristics of the offspring and explain how it is passed from parents to offspring.</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Short answer</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[3]</div>
  </div>
  <textarea placeholder="Write your answer here..."></textarea>
  <button class="submit-btn" onclick="showModelAnswer(this, '• The molecule is DNA [1]\n• The offspring receives some DNA from the male parent (in sperm) and some from the female parent (in egg cell) [1]\n• This DNA is contained in the chromosomes within the nucleus and determines the characteristics of the offspring [1]')">Show model answer</button>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q12">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">12</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">An alien scientist observes a crystal of salt growing in size. The scientist suggests that the salt crystal must be alive because it shows growth. Evaluate this suggestion, referring to at least <strong>three</strong> other characteristics of living organisms.</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Extended writing</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[4]</div>
  </div>
  <textarea style="min-height:110px;" placeholder="Write your answer here..."></textarea>
  <button class="submit-btn" onclick="showModelAnswer(this, 'The suggestion is incorrect / growth alone is not sufficient evidence of life [1]. To be considered living, an organism must show ALL characteristics. The salt crystal does NOT:\n• Carry out nutrition / obtain food for energy [1]\n• Carry out respiration / release energy from food [1]\n• Reproduce / make copies of itself [1]\n• Respond to stimuli in its environment [1]\n• Excrete metabolic waste products [1]\n(any 3 of the above for full marks)')">Show model answer</button>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q13">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">13</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">Which of the following statements about movement in living organisms is <strong>correct</strong>?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q13','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> Only animals are capable of movement</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q13','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> Plants cannot move any of their parts</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q13','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> All living organisms move in some way, though animals show locomotion more typically</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q13','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> Locomotion is the only type of movement recognised in living organisms</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q13"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q14">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">14</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">In humans, which waste product is produced when proteins are broken down, and through which organ is it eliminated?</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Multiple choice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[1]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="options">
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q14','A')"><span class="option-letter">A</span> Carbon dioxide — eliminated through the lungs</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q14','B')"><span class="option-letter">B</span> Urea — eliminated through the kidneys in urine</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q14','C')"><span class="option-letter">C</span> Oxygen — eliminated through the skin</div>
    <div class="option" onclick="mcq(this,'q14','D')"><span class="option-letter">D</span> Urea — eliminated through the liver in bile</div>
  </div>
  <div class="feedback" id="fb-q14"></div>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q15">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">15</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
      <div class="q-text">Animals are described as <em>heterotrophic</em>. Explain what this means and state how animals obtain energy compared to plants.</div>
      <span class="q-type-badge">Short answer</span>
    </div>
    <div class="q-marks">[2]</div>
  </div>
  <textarea placeholder="Write your answer here..."></textarea>
  <button class="submit-btn" onclick="showModelAnswer(this, '• Heterotrophic means obtaining food from a range of different (external) sources [1]\n• Animals eat other organisms (plants or animals) and obtain energy from the complex molecules in food; they cannot make their own food from sunlight as plants do [1]')">Show model answer</button>
</div>

<div class="question" id="q16">
  <div class="q-header">
    <div class="q-num">16</div>
    <div style="flex:1">
